**issue (behavior, blocking):** `super.focus()` also runs when no option is focusable, so the group gets `focus-ring` while DOM focus stays outside, the same state as in #13456. The `disabled` guard does not cover this, for example a `readonly` radio group with no value (all radio buttons are disabled), or a checkbox group where every checkbox is disabled. Same at `packages/checkbox-group/src/vaadin-checkbox-group-mixin.js:98`.

```js
if (target) {
  target.focus(options);
  super.focus(options);
}
```

Please add a test: `readonly` radio group without value, call `focus()`, expect no `focus-ring` and unchanged `document.activeElement`.
